  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water as Leverage Academy USA &#x2013; Scoping in preparation of decision-making for WaL Academy USA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water as Leverage (WaL) is an inclusive, design-led approach to urban water resilience that reframes water challenges as opportunities for transformation. Initiated by the Dutch government, WaL connects communities, governments, financiers, and designers to co-create integrated solutions that are socially just, ecologically sound, and economically viable.As part of the Dutch government&#x2019;s commitment to the United Nations (UN) 2023 Water Action Agenda, the ambition of this assignment, in close collaboration with the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and the Netherlands Ministry of Infrastructure and Water Management, is to build on the momentum of Water as Leverage (WaL) and explore opportunities for scaling up its approach in the United States (USA). The assignment will focus on a quick-scan scoping of a potential WaL Academy USA, assessing its added value and outlining a first conceptual design. Anchored in the broader WaL ambition - comprising the institutionalisation of WaL through the WaL Factory, the strengthening of knowledge and innovation via the WaL Academy, and the implementation of tangible WaL City Initiatives, the WaL Academy USA could provide a platform to inspire and accelerate locally owned initiatives, whilst also derive lessons-learned for the Netherlands. By sharing WaL experiences and introducing the WaL+A collaboration model, it aims to foster integral, inclusive, and transformative project development that enhances urban water resilience and long-term impact.</narrative>
  </description>
